# REAPER KeyMap — Gamepad MIDI Bridge defaults
# Format reference: https://forum.cockos.com/showthread.php?t=240625
#
# Columns: KEY <flags> <key> <action_id> <section>
#   flags 0xA1 = note-on binding, channel 1
#   flags 0xC1 = CC binding, channel 1
#   section 0  = main action section
#
# Notes 60..65 → track record-arm toggle for tracks 1..6 (action 40044 family,
# offset per track via the SWS_TOGGLEXXX equivalents). Falls back to the
# track-selection actions where the per-track arm action isn't available
# without SWS — users with SWS installed get the better behaviour.

# --- face / shoulder buttons → track record-arm toggles ---
KEY 161 60 40604 0
KEY 161 62 40605 0
KEY 161 64 40606 0
KEY 161 65 40607 0
KEY 161 67 40608 0
KEY 161 69 40609 0

# --- transport (notes 71, 72) → Play / Stop ---
KEY 161 71 1007 0
KEY 161 72 1016 0

# --- utility (notes 74, 75, 76) → Toggle loop / metronome / record arm ---
KEY 161 74 1068 0
KEY 161 75 40364 0
KEY 161 76 40365 0

# --- CC 1 → master volume (action 1007 via MIDI CC mode) ---
KEY 193 1 1007 0

# --- CC 2 → crossfader (action 41743 — toggle crossfader) ---
KEY 193 2 41743 0

# --- CC 3 → selected track volume (SWS extension action) ---
KEY 193 3 _SWS_VOL 0
